    "verdict": "reject",
    "blockers": [
        {
            "claim": "Dropped frame reporting is completely removed, breaking error propagation. The code that reported drops from the worker path (onFrame) was deleted, the notifyDropped() method was removed, and the m_dropNotifyPending atomic was removed. Dropped frames are now silently lost.",
            "file": "app/qttunebridge.cpp",
            "quote": "self->m_droppedFrames.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);\n        return;"
        },
        {
            "claim": "Defensive buffer length clamp was removed, creating potential buffer overrun. The old code clamped data_length to sizeof(frame->data) before passing to QByteArray, but the new code uses frame->data_length directly without validation.",
            "file": "app/qttunebridge.cpp",
            "quote": "vm[\"payloadHex\"] = QByteArray(\n        reinterpret_cast<const char*>(frame->data),\n        static_cast<qsizetype>(frame->data_length)).toHex();"
        },
        {
            "claim": "Signal decode uses hardcoded 8-byte length instead of actual payload length, breaking CAN-FD / short frame support. The comment claims the opposite of what the code does.",
            "file": "app/qttunebridge.cpp",
            "quote": "if (qttune_decode_signal(&def, frame->data, 8, &val) == 0) {"
        },
        {
            "claim": "Staging buffer is cleared instead of merged, breaking coalescing behavior. The old code merged signal values across frames within the 100ms window; the new code clears and rebuilds per frame.",
            "file": "app/qttunebridge.cpp",
            "quote": "m_stagingBuffer.clear();"
        },
        {
            "claim": "Include for qttune/signals.h was removed from header, potentially breaking compilation if QttuneSignalSet is defined there. The implementation uses static_cast to QttuneSignalSet* but there's no declaration visible.",
            "file": "app/qttunebridge.h",
            "quote": "#include \"qttune/core.h\""
        }
    ],
    "questions": [
        "Where is QttuneSignalSet defined? If it's in qttune/signals.h, removing that include will cause compilation failure.",
        "Is the void* parameter in setSignalSet intentional as an opaque handle pattern, or is this a mistaken change? The comment says 'FIX: typed parameter' but the code uses void*.",
        "What is the intended behavior for the staging buffer? The proposal says 'rebuilt per frame' but the old code had merge logic for coalescing.",
        "How should dropped frame reporting work now that notifyDropped() was removed?"
    ],
    "nits": [
        "Remove the misleading comment '// qttunebridge.cpp' that was added to clearFrames().",
        "Add back the defensive clamp for data_length or add explicit validation.",
